  "reason": "Protects what the docs tell a human about the opt-in touchbard device run: ADR-0014 records legacy KMS over atomic, sysfs card identity before open, DRM master ownership, an inactive-only prior state, that a KMS success is only a submitted frame because the driver discards flush/clear results, and the options not taken; docs/hil-checklist.md gains a device-run section with the TB-28/TB-9 seat and ownership preconditions, --drm/--touch as opt-in with VERIFIED_DIGITIZERS empty until TB-45, TB-10 display vs TB-45 digitizer evidence, source-only facts vs unobserved ones, refusal of an active foreign state, an attempted and reported restore, no promise after SIGKILL/unplug/power loss, the hardware-runbook return and human evidence afterwards; GLOSSARY.md defines Touch Bar card, Digitizer profile and Restore. Checks match meaning per paragraph, item or row, not exact wording. Checks named preserve-* guard text already written (ADR-0014 digitizer/signal/unsafe decisions, Digitizer and Cancelled touch) and the privacy rules; the rest were red at base 01dbc59.",
